          <span class="ti-title">Order 2026-120 &mdash; Land Use Ordinance: Data Center Ban (First Reading)</span>
          <span class="ti-brief">Prohibits data centers citywide, following a 180-day moratorium.</span>
        </span>
        <span class="ti-chev">+</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="ti-body">
        <p>Data centers are currently permitted only within Contract Zone 12 (the Rock Row Contract Zone). Following a council-adopted 180-day moratorium on new data center projects (effective June 1, 2026) and a unanimous Planning Board recommendation, this amendment prohibits data centers as a principal use citywide (server rooms supporting other businesses remain allowed). Mayor Morse spoke in support, citing water/electricity demand, utility costs, noise, and infrastructure concerns.</p>
        <span class="tldw-decision">&#10003; Passed first reading, unanimous show of hands.</span>
        <p class="label">Action item</p>
        <ul><li>Public hearing and second reading &mdash; Assignee: Council | Deadline: November 2, 2026.</li></ul>
      </div>
